# Cloudflare static-assets headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/).
# Vite copies this file from public/ to dist/_headers. GitHub Pages ignores it, which is why
# multi-threaded Stockfish only runs on Cloudflare; see docs/deploy.md.
#
# Cross-origin isolation (COOP + COEP) is what unlocks SharedArrayBuffer, which the
# multi-threaded engine needs (src/engine/capabilities.ts reads crossOriginIsolated).
# COEP is `require-corp` rather than `credentialless`: Safari does not implement
# `credentialless`, and `require-corp` costs us nothing because every cross-origin request the
# app makes is a CORS `fetch()` (lichess.org, explorer.lichess.ovh, api.chess.com, which all
# send CORS headers) or Google Fonts (which sends Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin).
# If an <img> or <iframe> from another origin is ever added, it must be CORP/CORS-enabled.
#
# CSP, directive by directive:
#   default-src 'self'          everything not listed below is same-origin only.
#   script-src                  'self' + 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for Stockfish WebAssembly (no JS eval).
#                               The sha256 is the inline theme bootstrap in index.html, which must
#                               run before first paint; `node scripts/check-headers.mjs` fails the build if
#                               that script changes without this hash being updated.
#   worker-src 'self' blob:     engine, CSV/PGN workers and the service worker are same-origin; blob:
#                               covers Emscripten's pthread workers.
#   style-src                   'unsafe-inline' is needed because Radix and friends inject <style>
#                               elements at runtime and React sets style="" attributes. Styles cannot
#                               run script, so this is the accepted trade. Google Fonts CSS is allowed.
#   font-src / img-src          fonts.gstatic.com; piece sets and icons are same-origin, data:/blob:
#                               for generated board art and exported images.
#   connect-src                 EXACT list of external APIs the code calls: lichess.org (game import,
#                               src/features/library/providers.ts), explorer.lichess.ovh (masters
#                               explorer, src/features/analysis/explorer.ts), api.chess.com (game
#                               import). Deliberately NOT `https:`: the bring-your-own-key coach
#                               (S21) will need user-chosen endpoints, and this line is widened in
#                               the PR that ships it, so the tight policy stands until then.
#   frame-ancestors 'none'      nobody may embed the app (clickjacking). Also X-Frame-Options for
#                               old browsers. object-src, base-uri and form-action are closed.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-IJl/6T5XzN9SHAJnyA0O2Cuh7z1Ab2YzbOM5i8rw4NA='; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://lichess.org https://explorer.lichess.ovh https://api.chess.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()

# Hashed build output never changes under its name.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The worker and the shell must always revalidate or an update can never land.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
